# The one LFS rule this repository has ever needed.
docs/server_selection/request_load_scenes/fixed20_observations.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Batch files must arrive as CRLF on every machine, not only on the ones whose user
# set core.autocrlf=true. cmd.exe parses the label/goto-dense launchers wrongly when
# they come out of a clone with LF endings, and the failure is silent and depends on
# the cloner's git config rather than on anything in the repository.
#
# Measured on the committed blobs before this rule existed: launcher.bat and
# start_dashboard.bat are stored LF (163 and 4 bare-LF lines, no CRLF at all), while
# docs/make.bat is stored CRLF - so the repository disagreed with itself about which
# convention batch files use, and only a working copy with autocrlf=true ever saw
# working launchers. `text eol=crlf` fixes the checkout for both conventions at once, so
# docs/make.bat is deliberately left as it is: re-normalising an upstream Sphinx file to
# buy nothing but a tidier index would inflate this repository's diff against upstream,
# which is a number the project tracks on purpose.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
